          "body": "Fixed with revision 502263.\n",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=reschke",
            "name": "reschke",
            "key": "reschke",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677"
            },
            "displayName": "Julian Reschke",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "created": "2007-02-01T16:31:17.092+0000",
          "updated": "2007-02-01T16:31:17.092+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12361766/comment/12469519",
          "id": "12469519",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=jukkaz",
            "name": "jukkaz",
            "key": "jukkaz",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130"
            },
            "displayName": "Jukka Zitting",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "> A related question is what our expectation is for JCR implementations. Are they\n> allowed to reject something that doesn't parse as a URI according to RFC3986?\n\nI don't recall the JCR spec saying anything about this, but since XML namespace (http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-xml-names/) names are RFC 3986 URIs, I think it would be perfectly OK for a repository implementatino to only allow valid URIs. One concrete benefit of such a policy would be the avoidance of invalid namespace names in XML exports. In fact we may even want to consider enforcing this in Jackrabbit.\n\nPS. The \"www.apache.org/...\" name can actually be interpreted as a relative URI, and is only deprecated but not strictly prohibited by the current XML namespace spec.\n",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=jukkaz",
            "name": "jukkaz",
            "key": "jukkaz",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130"
            },
            "displayName": "Jukka Zitting",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "created": "2007-02-01T17:38:34.242+0000",
          "updated": "2007-02-01T17:38:34.242+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12361766/comment/12469521",
          "id": "12469521",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=reschke",
            "name": "reschke",
            "key": "reschke",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677"
            },
            "displayName": "Julian Reschke",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "body": "Just a nit: \"www.apache.org/...\" is a relative reference (<http://greenbytes.de/tech/webdav/rfc3986.html#rfc.section.4.2>), but not a URI (<http://greenbytes.de/tech/webdav/rfc3986.html#rfc.section.3>).\n",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=reschke",
            "name": "reschke",
            "key": "reschke",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677"
            },
            "displayName": "Julian Reschke",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "created": "2007-02-01T17:47:25.618+0000",
          "updated": "2007-02-01T17:47:25.618+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12361766/comment/12473543",
          "id": "12473543",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=jukkaz",
            "name": "jukkaz",
            "key": "jukkaz",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130"
            },
            "displayName": "Jukka Zitting",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "Thanks for the terminology update! The devil's in the details...\n\nThe XML namespace spec says: \"An XML namespace is identified by a URI reference [RFC3986]\", meaning both full URIs and relative URI references. The current version adds a note that deprecates the use of relative URI references.\n\nThe JCR spec somewhat vaguely says: \"Namespacing in a content repository is patterned after namespacing in XML. As in XML, the prefix is actually shorthand for the full namespace, which is a URI.\"\n\nIt seems fair to interpret this as meaning that only full URIs are allowed as JCR namespaces.\n",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=jukkaz",
            "name": "jukkaz",
            "key": "jukkaz",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130"
            },
            "displayName": "Jukka Zitting",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
